        "original_id": "1d176d3a-7139-5972-b39e-ed0e9b0435b7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tommy Faile\n- Places: Brown Mountain, North Carolina, Wiseman's View, Linville Falls\n- Works: \"Phantom 309\", \"The Legend of the Brown Mountain Lights\"\n- Topics: Brown Mountain Lights, ghost lights\n\nFacts:\n- Tommy Faile was born on September 15, 1928, and he was an American songwriter and singer.\n- Tommy Faile was best known for composing \"Phantom 309\" and singing \"The Legend of the Brown Mountain Lights.\"\n- The Brown Mountain Lights are a series of ghost lights reported near Brown Mountain in North Carolina.\n- Wiseman's View is one of the best vantage points for seeing the Brown Mountain Lights, and it is about 4 miles from Linville Falls, North Carolina.\n- Tommy Faile died on August 2, 1998.",
